ration issues. Which is more severe? Memory for numbers is a safety-critical technical issue. Nasty remarks also crew. A's issues are interpersonal, could be mitigated with training. A's strengths are safety-critical (anticipation, spatial vision). So likely A is better overall. So we can shift to Candidate A.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 2's points and maybe bring additional evidence: A's anticipation of dangerous situations, leadership, spatial vision. Also note that A's \"not good at taking criticism\" is a concern but perhaps less safety-critical than B's weak numeric memory. So we can say we now support Candidate A.\n\nThus public message: I agree with Agent 2 that A's safety strengths outweigh B's issues, and I shift my vote to A. Provide reasoning.\n\nMetadata JSON: vote Candidate A.\n\nProceed."}
